# Day 28/50 — Multitasking

Listening to music while browsing the internet, downloading a file while attending a video call.
It feels like a computer is doing everything at once.

This is called **multitasking**

An operating system manages multiple tasks by switching CPU time between processes or threads
On multi-core systems, some tasks can also execute simultaneously.

The result? We can use multiple applications without having to finish one before starting another.

But there's a catch.
Managing many tasks also requires coordination and resources.

Maybe doing more things isn't always the same as doing them well.

**Because multitasking is not just about handling everything. It's about managing everything without losing control**
